{"sounds":{"intro":"Ukrainian uses Cyrillic, but it differs from Russian in a few letters and sounds. Learn these first.","rows":[["і","ee, like \"see\"","ліс (lees)"],["и","\"ih\", like the \"i\" in \"bit\"","мир (mihr)"],["ї","yee","їжа (YEE-zhah)"],["є","ye, like \"yes\"","є (ye)"],["г","h, soft breathy (not \"g\")","гора (hoh-RAH)"],["ґ","g, hard, rare letter","ґанок (GAH-nok)"],["е","eh","мене (meh-NEH)"],["щ","shch","щастя (SHCHAHS-tyah)"],["ь","soft sign: softens the consonant before it","день (den')"],["'","apostrophe: hard break before я, ю, є, ї","м'ясо (MYAH-so)"],["ч","ch","час (chahs)"],["ж","zh","жінка (ZHEEN-kah)"],["в","v (at the end of a word or before a consonant it sounds close to \"w\")","вода (voh-DAH)"],["о","oh (unstressed it is still \"o\", not \"a\" as in Russian)","молоко (moh-loh-KOH)"]],"notes":["Unlike Russian, Ukrainian has no \"ы\" and \"э\" and \"ё\". Unstressed \"о\" stays \"o\".","Nouns have 3 genders and 7 cases (including a vocative: used to call someone, Мамо! Друже!). Start without the cases."]},"numbers":[{"id":"0-to-10","title":"0 to 10","items":[["zero","нуль","nool'"],["one","один","oh-DEEN"],["two","два","dvah"],["three","три","trih"],["four","чотири","choh-TIH-rih"],["five","п'ять","pyaht'"],["six","шість","sheest'"],["seven","сім","seem"],["eight","вісім","VEE-seem"],["nine","дев'ять","DEH-vyaht'"],["ten","десять","DEH-syat'"]]},{"id":"11-to-20","title":"11 to 20","items":[["eleven","одинадцять","oh-dih-NAHD-tsyat'"],["twelve","дванадцять","dvah-NAHD-tsyat'"],["thirteen","тринадцять","trih-NAHD-tsyat'"],["fourteen","чотирнадцять","choh-tihr-NAHD-tsyat'"],["fifteen","п'ятнадцять","pyat-NAHD-tsyat'"],["sixteen","шістнадцять","sheest-NAHD-tsyat'"],["seventeen","сімнадцять","seem-NAHD-tsyat'"],["eighteen","вісімнадцять","vee-seem-NAHD-tsyat'"],["nineteen","дев'ятнадцять","deh-vyat-NAHD-tsyat'"],["twenty","двадцять","DVAHD-tsyat'"]]},{"id":"tens-and-big-numbers","title":"Tens and big numbers","items":[["twenty-one","двадцять о